WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:06.773
[music playing]

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.109
NARRATOR: I'm losing daylight.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.312
This is an expanse
of grassland and it

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.013
has what I need for a shelter.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.285
And all this grass that
I'm going to cut down,

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:23.790
I'm going to either turn into
my bed or use for my roof.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.192
Hits the rainy
season which means,

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.660
you better count on it raining.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.767
No.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.502
Wait.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.871
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.173
I cannot believe this.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.579
While I was chopping I
chopped up a clump of grass

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:51.418
and under the dirt clod, I just
saw this little bit of color.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:55.054
I would have never
thought in my entire life

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.992
I would see one of
these in real life.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:03.730
This is a blind worm snake.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.832
It has a little
flickering tongue

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.333
as it's a digging machine.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.337
It uses this its nose which
is one big large hard scale.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.840
And it uses it like
a shovel or a wedge

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:18.411
and it's able to dig through the
ground and look for its prey.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.047
NARRATOR: It's a
seven-striped blind snake,

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.216
a truly bizarre species.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.452
It spends its life
deep underground.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.787
So sightings are
incredibly rare.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:31.524
When you're out here, you're
up to your knees in mud.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.027
You have funguses
and parasites and all

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.362
the wounds that get infected.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.964
The rain.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:43.336
If you don't love these little
things like this along the way,

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.138
this place would destroy you.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.944
NARRATOR: Here just a few
100 miles from the equator,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.546
the light goes
out like a switch.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.849
I've got to get
back to my shelter.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.218
[music playing]

